      {
        "id": 2637840491,
        "content": "Same issue that held back `telegram-kernel` [here](https://github.com/ubiquity-os-marketplace/ubiquity-os-kernel-telegram/pull/23#issuecomment-2445376992)\r\nIn that case, the secret was pushed to the worker directly from org secrets via a workflow which I had no control over and these vars were being used to auth via `Octokit/App`. In my case the error was logged through the worker and not posted.\r\nI'm a little rusty but I recall that in a `.env` file the PK had to be a single string, whereas in GH secrets/workers you'd replace `\\n` with line breaks. Hope this helps.",
